                                            Style="{StaticResource SecondaryButtonStyle}"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_GenerateANewNtfyTopic}"
                                            Click="OnGenerateNtfyTopicClick"
                                            ToolTip="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_MakesAFreshRandomTopic}" />
                                </Grid>
                                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_Server}" FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}" Foreground="{DynamicResource WhiteBrush}" Margin="0,6,0,2" />
                                <TextBox x:Name="NtfyServerInput" AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_NtfyServerAddress}" Padding="8,6" FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                         Background="{DynamicResource NavyBrush}"
                                         LostFocus="OnNtfyServerCommitted" Style="{StaticResource AppTextBoxStyle}"
                                         ToolTip="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_LeaveAsNtfyShUnless}" />
                                <TextBlock x:Name="PhoneNtfyVerdict" FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <Button x:Name="PhoneTestButton" Content="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_TestMyPhone}" Padding="12,5" Margin="0,8,0,0"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Left" Visibility="Collapsed"
                                    Style="{StaticResource SecondaryStrongButtonStyle}" FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                    AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_SendATestNotificationTo}"
                                    Click="OnPhoneTestClick" />

                            <!-- F-094. Every arm of this line used to be CyanBrush — the accent, which
                                 is the treatment a SUCCESS gets — so "your webhook was deleted, so
                                 nothing is reaching your phone" rendered identically to "sending to
                                 #alerts". The sentence said one thing and the styling said another,
                                 and styling is what gets read first.

                                 The failure arms take RowExpiredAccentBrush and the "▲ " prefix, which
                                 is the pair MainWindow already uses for the compat and Bloxstrap
                                 banners. Driven from a Tag rather than assigned in code-behind so the
                                 colour stays visible to the theme gates — code-behind colour
                                 assignment is exactly the blind spot F-098 records. -->
                            <TextBlock x:Name="AlertsStatusLine" FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}" Margin="0,10,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                <TextBlock.Style>
                                    <Style TargetType="TextBlock">
                                        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CyanBrush}" />
                                        <Style.Triggers>
                                            <Trigger Property="Tag" Value="failure">
                                                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource RowExpiredAccentBrush}" />
                                            </Trigger>
                                        </Style.Triggers>
                                    </Style>
                                </TextBlock.Style>
                            </TextBlock>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>

                    <!-- Memory (F-023, spec 4.1). These four have been persisted since v1.13 and
                         referenced by zero .xaml until now: a page named "Alerts & memory" shipped
                         with no memory controls on it, and the only way to change one was Notepad.
                         SettingsReachabilityTests is the fence that makes that shape fail a build.

                         WHY FREE TEXT AND NOT A PRESET PICKER, since the idle threshold two cards
                         up is a ComboBox. A picker cannot produce an out-of-range value, so it
                         cannot satisfy prd Story 1.1's requirement that one be refused VISIBLY —
                         the criterion would be unfalsifiable by construction. Free text is what
                         gives the refusal something to refuse. It is also what "hand-editing
                         settings.json still works" already implies: the file accepts any integer,
                         so the UI has to be able to show any integer and reject the wrong ones.

                         Blank is not empty, it is "RoRoRo picks". SettingsBlob.MemoryReserveMb and
                         SettingsBlob.MemoryCapMb are int? and null means never set — App.xaml.cs
                         derives from installed RAM via MemoryDefaults. An empty box has to
                         round-trip back to null or a user who clears one silently pins whatever
                         happened to be showing.

                         WRITE THOSE TWO NAMES DOTTED, HERE AND IN THE CODE-BEHIND, and do not tidy
                         the owner off. SettingsReachabilityTests' control edge matches a bare
                         setting name anywhere in an App .cs/.xaml file, comments included, and its
                         one exclusion is a preceding "." (a member read is a consumer, not a
                         control). So a bare setting name in a sentence is enough to report that
                         setting reachable; the same name written with its owner is not. Proved on
                         2026-08-10: with all three of the projection setting's sites renamed away,
                         the fence still passed on two doc comments alone. Qualified names keep the
                         fence measuring the controls. -->

                    <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_Memory}"
                               Style="{StaticResource SectionHeadingStyle}"
                               AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_Memory}"
                               AutomationProperties.HeadingLevel="Level2" />
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorderStyle}">
                        <StackPanel>
                            <StackPanel>
                                <CheckBox x:Name="MemoryWatchdogEnabledToggle"
                                          Foreground="{DynamicResource WhiteBrush}"
                                          FontSize="{DynamicResource HeadingFontSize}"
                                          FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                          AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WatchMemoryWhileAccountsAre}"
                                          Click="OnMemoryWatchdogEnabledToggle">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WatchMemoryWhileAccountsAre_2}" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                                </CheckBox>
                                <TextBlock FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                           Margin="22,4,0,0"
                                           Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_RororoChecksEveryRunningClient}" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <!-- WHAT BLANK ACTUALLY PICKS, on this machine, said out loud (item 4a).
                                 The three boxes below accept blank to mean "RoRoRo picks one" and
                                 said nothing about what it picked, which is this cycle's own defect
                                 restated: the app knew and did not say.

                                 The text is set from the code-behind rather than written here,
                                 because the figures are DERIVED and the derivation must be the one
                                 App.WireMemoryWatchdogAsync already runs. See
                                 AutomaticMemorySummary — it calls MemoryDefaults, so a number here
                                 cannot disagree with the number the watchdog uses. A literal in
                                 this markup would be a second source of truth for a value that
                                 changes with the PC it runs on.

                                 Muted prose, not the warning vocabulary, even on the probe-failure
                                 path. A machine whose RAM cannot be read is a standing fact, not an
                                 event, and MemorySettingsWarning below is where a refusal speaks.
                                 Painting a permanent line in the warning accent would shout on
                                 every open and leave the actual refusal nothing louder to be. -->
                            <TextBlock x:Name="AutomaticMemoryLine"
                                       FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                       Margin="0,14,0,0"
                                       AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WhatRororoPicksWhenA}" />

                            <!-- Row separation is a call-site margin, same as the Startup card. -->
                            <StackPanel Margin="0,14,0,0">
                                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_MemoryToKeepFreeMb}"
                                           FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource WhiteBrush}"
                                           Margin="0,0,0,4" />
                                <!-- Blank means "RoRoRo picks" — and the pick is now IN the box as a
                                     ghost (Este, 2026-09-05): a blank field looked like nothing was
                                     happening. The ghost is the same MemoryDefaults figure the intro
                                     sentence quotes, hidden the moment real text exists. -->
                                <Grid Width="184" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                                <TextBox x:Name="MemoryReserveMbInput"
                                         Padding="8,6"
                                         FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                         Background="{DynamicResource NavyBrush}"
                                         Style="{StaticResource AppTextBoxStyle}"
                                         AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_MemoryToKeepFreeIn}"
                                         AutomationProperties.HelpText="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_AWholeNumberFrom256}"
                                         LostFocus="OnMemoryReserveCommitted"
                                         TextChanged="OnMemoryInputTextChanged" />
                                <TextBlock x:Name="MemoryReserveGhost"
                                           FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                           Margin="10,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                           IsHitTestVisible="False" />
                                </Grid>
                                <TextBlock FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                           Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                           Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_YouGetWarnedOnceFree}" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <StackPanel Margin="0,14,0,0">
                                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WarnWhenOneAccountPasses}"
                                           FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource WhiteBrush}"
                                           Margin="0,0,0,4" />
                                <Grid Width="184" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                                <TextBox x:Name="MemoryCapMbInput"
                                         Padding="8,6"
                                         FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                         Background="{DynamicResource NavyBrush}"
                                         Style="{StaticResource AppTextBoxStyle}"
                                         AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WarnWhenOneAccountPasses_2}"
                                         AutomationProperties.HelpText="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_AWholeNumberFrom256_2}"
                                         LostFocus="OnMemoryCapCommitted"
                                         TextChanged="OnMemoryInputTextChanged" />
                                <TextBlock x:Name="MemoryCapGhost"
                                           FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                           Margin="10,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                           IsHitTestVisible="False" />
                                </Grid>
                                <TextBlock FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                           Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                           Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_OneClientOnItsOwn}" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <StackPanel Margin="0,14,0,0">
                                <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WarnThisFarAheadMinutes}"
                                           FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource WhiteBrush}"
                                           Margin="0,0,0,4" />
                                <TextBox x:Name="ProjectionWarnMinutesInput"
                                         Width="120"
                                         HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                         Padding="8,6"
                                         FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                         Background="{DynamicResource NavyBrush}"
                                         Style="{StaticResource AppTextBoxStyle}"
                                         AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_WarnThisManyMinutesAhead}"
                                         AutomationProperties.HelpText="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_AWholeNumberOfMinutes}"
                                         LostFocus="OnProjectionWarnCommitted" />
                                <TextBlock FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                           Margin="0,4,0,0"
                                           Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_RororoWatchesHowFastYour}" />
                            </StackPanel>

                            <!-- This section's OWN failure line, and the three reasons it is its
                                 own (spec 5). It is not AlertsStatusLine: that line is CyanBrush,
                                 belongs to the Alerts card above, and spec 5 explicitly leaves it
                                 alone. It is not the Theme section's line: that one does not exist
                                 yet and reports a different thing.

                                 RowExpiredAccentBrush and the U+25B2 prefix are the warning
                                 vocabulary v1.17 established across expired rows, idle chips,
                                 memory chips and the compat banner. A fifth warning surface speaks
                                 it. Cyan is the accent — the same treatment a SUCCESS would get —
                                 so a refusal painted cyan would look like a save.

                                 Collapsed until something is refused. A status line that speaks on
                                 every save is noise, and the refusal has to arrive as a change. -->
                            <TextBlock x:Name="MemorySettingsWarning"
                                       FontSize="{DynamicResource BodyFontSize}"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource RowExpiredAccentBrush}"
                                       TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                       Margin="0,12,0,0"
                                       Visibility="Collapsed"
                                       AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_MemorySettingsWarning}"
                                       AutomationProperties.LiveSetting="Assertive" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>
                </StackPanel>

                <StackPanel x:Name="PageDiscord" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <!-- v1.14+ Discord presence + Join (plan 2026-08-03). Off by default; the status
                         line reports the live connection state in plain words, never a stack trace. -->
                    <TextBlock Text="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_DiscordPresence}"
                               Style="{StaticResource SectionHeadingStyle}"
                               AutomationProperties.Name="{loc:Loc SettingsPage_DiscordPresence}"
                               AutomationProperties.HeadingLevel="Level2" />
                    <Border Style="{StaticResource CardBorderStyle}">
                        <StackPanel>
                            <CheckBox x:Name="DiscordPresenceToggle"
